I realize that in my example, c("A", "A", "A") is classified as different than c("B", "B", "B") because different names are assigned, even though the clustering is the same. Depending on the cluster names you input, this may or may not be a problem. However if you replace fixed = sort(uniques)[ints[x]] with fixed = ints[x], both would be renamed to c(1, 1, 1), and all your unique vectors will have cluster numbers, rather than cluster names.
