Hi, Kristina,  I have not used the MonteCarlo feature for the ctree function.  I can't tell from your description whether any of your predictors have null values (where one or more records have incomplete predictor info), or whether you simply have an unbalanced design (where all records have complete predictor info, but you just have uneven numbers of records per categorical level).  I doubt that the latter situation would cause that problem (I've used it with unbalanced designs without any apparent issue), but I think I remember encountering situations (outside of ctree) where you couldn't use Monte Carlo when there were null values.  I don't recall the specifics offhand though.  J.

